-- title:
--   Minimal primes over p in a stalk are the two branch ideals
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \ge 1$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ that becomes $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ (with $M/p$ nonzero), and the hypothesis $hj$ that the $q$-expansion $jqModC$ of $j$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ lies in the intermediate field $qExpFunctionFieldC$ of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ attached to the full group $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a term of `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, the bundle of Deligne–Rapoport-type data and properties for the model of $X_H(M)$ over $R\,p$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and $\rho : R\,p \to A$ a ring map inducing the structure map $R\,p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a map $\rho_O : R\,p \to O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, such that the pullback scheme $X_O =$ `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO` (the fibre product of the structure morphism `toBase` with $\operatorname{Spec} \rho_O$) is integral, together with $O \to \kappa_A$ compatible with $\rho$. Let $x \in X_O$ have Noetherian local ring, and assume both distinguished points $\mathfrak{X}.\xi_{\inf}$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\xi_{\mathrm{zero}}$ (built from these data) specialise to $x$. Write $P_\infty, P_0 \subseteq \mathcal{O}_{X_O,x}$ for the pullbacks of the maximal ideals of the stalks at those two points along the specialisation maps. Then $P_\infty$ and $P_0$ are prime and contain the image of $p$; every minimal prime over the ideal $(p)$ of $\mathcal{O}_{X_O,x}$ equals $P_\infty$ or $P_0$; and every prime of height $1$ containing $p$ equals $P_\infty$ or $P_0$.
--
--   This is the local form, at a point of the model of $X_H(M)$ over a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $p$, of the statement that the special fibre has exactly the two Deligne–Rapoport branches through a crossing point: the only codimension-one specialisations of $x$ inside the fibre over $p$ are the two branch generic points. It feeds the identification of the intersection $P_\infty \cap P_0$ with the ideal generated by $p$ in [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.branchIdeal_xiInf_inf_branchIdeal_xiZero_eq_span_baseGerm`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.branchIdeal_xiInf_inf_branchIdeal_xiZero_eq_span_baseGerm).
